# CReplxx — vendored replxx

Upstream: https://github.com/AmokHuginnsson/replxx
Pinned commit: 1f149bfe20bf6e49c1afd4154eaf0032c8c2fda2 (DEPENDENCIES.md candidate [S09])
Licence: replxx/LICENSE.md (BSD-style, copyright retained, unmodified)
C++ standard: C++11 (upstream CMakeLists); threads via libpthread.

Files in `replxx/` are upstream sources from the pinned commit
(headers, .cxx sources, ConvertUTF.cpp, wcwidth.cpp), PLUS the
registered local patches below. Only these bridge/support files are
Needletail's: `include/shim.h`, `include/module.modulemap`,
`SHA256SUMS-upstream`, `patches/*.patch`, this file.

Provenance model (tree == upstream + registered patches):
- `SHA256SUMS-upstream` records the pristine upstream blob hashes.
- `patches/` holds each local deviation as a reviewed unified diff
  (one file per patch, repo-rooted a/ b/ paths). No other tree edit
  under `replxx/` is permitted.
- `./dev vendor-check` verifies both directions per patch: the tree
  file minus the patch hashes to the upstream manifest entry, and the
  patch applied to those pristine bytes reproduces the tree file
  byte-for-byte. The upstream manifest itself is never rewritten to
  bless a tree edit.
- Upstream ref `ThirdParty/replxx` (a full clone used for the
  secondary comparison) is gitignored and never committed.

## Registered patches (each independently reviewed)

1. `patches/0001-bracketed-paste-decode-lf.patch` →
   `replxx/replxx_impl.cxx` (`bracketed_paste`): decode pasted
   `KEY::control('J')` (LF) back to `'\n'`. Terminal::read_char
   control-maps C0 bytes; the paste path converted CR and TAB but not
   LF, so a pasted newline arrived as the out-of-range key code
   0x200004A and UTF-8-encoded as U+FFFD on output — multiline pastes
   lost every line break (found by M4-D PTY-02 development evidence).
   Mirrors the adjacent CR/TAB handling, same style. Required by
   COMPLETE-SPEC PTY-02 (exact submitted text).

Swift boundary: `shim.h` exposes only the C API (`extern "C"` in
replxx/replxx.h). C++ interoperability does not cross into Swift.
